DECISIONS APPLIED (walkthrough fleet-alt.1 spec pass, 2026-09-24). Drafted read-only at bde60be, BEFORE flight 4 landed (fleet-6gr: gate→hold/clear, `fleet hold`/`fleet clear`, [gates] split into [landing]/[permissions]/[guards.targets], routines evaluate the trigger; fleet-4j6: fleet.orders / fleet.run with v:1, label fleet:run; fleet-g68: PRD citations restated, PRDs archived; fleet-d11: dead flight code deleted). Every site cited here is RE-FOUND BY SYMBOL at pickup, and names from those beads are the landed ones. Every [ASSUMES Dn] in this spec was ruled as assumed by Alberto (AskUserQuestion, 2026-09-24). fleet-0q4 rulings in force: external adapters are one process per call; a run's record is written by a `run.set` verb (D2); the Actor type is defined in iex-a1 (D1).

SPEC (split d1 of fleet-0q4, drafted 2026-09-23).

**Behaviour.**
- The contract's checks move out of core/tests/contract.rs into core/src/store/conformance.rs, which is compiled into the binary so `fleet store check` (d2) can run it.
- Each check answers pass, fail-with-text, or skip-with-why. None panics.
- core/tests/contract.rs becomes the runner: one arm per check on the in-memory store, and one arm running every check on a real bd store made by the bd adapter's own `scratch`.
- This is fleet-6ravv.4's "one contract suite run against both stores". 6ravv.4 stays open for its other clause, moving the cli verb suites (cli/tests/{deliver,dispatch,run,item_json,seat,routines}.rs) off bd.

**Sites (at HEAD bde60be)**
- core/tests/contract.rs: 418 lines. The CHECKS table is at :41-53 (11 checks), the in-memory arms at :331-384, the real half at :390-397, and `the_table_names_every_check` at :402-418.
- core/tests/common/mod.rs:615-621 shared_store; :502-533 Scratch::new (bd init --prefix fx --quiet plus the test server args).
- core/tests/common/board.rs:63-97: bd_init_server_args and the private note_bd_init (the tools/dolt-test-server init count).
- core/src/test_support.rs: `unreadable: Option<String>` (:71) makes a store that answers nothing.

**Remedy**
1. core/src/store/conformance.rs:
   - `pub type Check = fn(&Ctx) -> Result<Passed, String>`, where `pub enum Passed { Pass, Skip(String) }` and `pub struct Ctx<'a> { pub store: &'a dyn Store, pub root: &'a Path, pub absent: &'a dyn Store }`. absent is the same adapter addressed at a directory holding no store;
   - `pub const CHECKS: &[(&str, Check)]`, in this order, because the first needs a fresh store:
     1. "empty listings": holds_open() == [], list(Ready) == [], list(Label("fleet-conformance-none")) == [];
     2. "version": the name and version are non-empty;
     3. "capabilities": an export, when present, passes validate();
     4. "create then show";
     5. "resolve by fragment": resolve(the suffix after the last '-', or the whole id) == id, and show(the same text).id == id;
     6. "missing is refused": resolve and show of "fleet-conformance-nobody-filed-this" are Refused, not Unreadable;
     7. "ambiguous is refused with candidates":
        - create items until two of this check's ids share a common substring s of their suffixes with s equal to neither suffix, up to 10 creates;
        - resolve(s) must be Refused, and its text must name both ids;
        - if resolve(s) answers Ok with an id whose suffix == s, try the next substring;
        - with no candidate after 10 creates, fail with "could not make an ambiguous fragment in 10 creates";
     8. "unreadable is could not tell": absent.show("x") and absent.list(Ready) are Unreadable, never Refused;
     9. "ready": a new item is in Ready; hold_raise takes it out; hold_clear brings it back; close takes it out;
     10. "label filter": a label unique to the check lists the item; close unlists it;
     11. "assignee filter": update assignee S (a fresh UUID v7 SeatId) lists it under S; it is still listed after close, with Status::Closed;
     12. "update": the title moves; the assignee sets; Update::unassigned reads None;
     13. "an order write keeps the run record" (from b5);
     14. "a run write keeps the order";
     15. "order.withdraw clears both";
     16. "timeline is append-only and ordered": three appends come back as the last three entries in order, with distinct ids and the kinds sent;
     17. "holds": raise lists it in holds_open; clear removes it; a second clear is Refused;
     18. "close": status Closed; a second close is Refused;
     19. "export": Skip("the store declares no export") when capabilities().export is None; otherwise today's export check;
   - `pub fn run(ctx: &Ctx) -> Vec<(&'static str, Result<Passed, String>)>` runs every check, never stopping at the first failure.
2. Scratch on bd:
   - Bd::capabilities answers scratch: true;
   - add to the trait `fn scratch(&self, into: &Path) -> Result<PathBuf, StoreError>`:
     - Bd runs `<bin> init --prefix fx --quiet` with current_dir(into), passing no server flag so the store is bd's embedded engine and never a server port, and answers into;
     - the fake answers into and sets scratch: true;
     - an adapter without the capability answers Unreadable("this store declares no scratch");
   - measure on bd 1.3.0 that `bd -C <empty temp dir> show x --json` is classified Unreadable by the bd adapter. If it reads as Missing through shown(), fix the classification in the bd adapter: an error naming no database or no .beads is Unreadable.
3. core/tests/contract.rs:
   - one `#[test]` per CHECKS entry on a fresh Board (absent = a FakeStore with unreadable set);
   - `every_check_holds_against_bd_too`: `Bd::at(shared_store("contract").root)`, with absent = Bd::at(an empty temp dir) and the test server kept;
   - `the_bd_adapter_makes_a_scratch_store_every_check_holds_on`: a temp dir, bd.scratch(dir), Bd::at(the answered root), run all; make `note_bd_init` pub in common/board.rs and call it once so tools/dolt-test-server's count stays true;
   - `the_table_names_every_check`: count `CHECKS` entries against the per-check arms, as today.
4. Delete the old check functions from contract.rs. The file keeps only arms.

**Acceptance**
1. Every per-check arm is green on the fake, and both real arms are green.
2. (Red-proof, arm "unreadable is could not tell") Against a fake whose unreadable read answers Refused, the check fails with a text naming the check. Show it.
3. (Red-proof, arm "an order write keeps the run record") Temporarily make the fake's order_set replace the whole metadata; the check fails.
4. `the_table_names_every_check` fails when an arm is added without a CHECKS entry. Keep its existing red-proof.
5. `fleet_core::store::conformance` has no `assert!` or `panic!` (grep).

Gate line: touched suites green; the reviewer runs the full suite, ran or cached, at landing.
Size estimate: ~500 changed lines (conformance ~330, contract.rs net about −100, bd/fake ~60).
