SPEC (split 4b of fleet-zlk, drafted 2026-09-23).
Names: (the shared names line above.)

Behaviour.
- Every item fact on the per-machine stream becomes ONE line kind, `item.entry`, with payload {item, entry, kind} and nothing else [ASSUMES D2]. It is written after the entry's read-back, as the events are at HEAD.
- `check.read` stays a machine event [ASSUMES D3].
- `run.cancelled` stays. cancel writes one signal per cleared entry.
- The controller's crash-cap latch asks the store, through the run seam, whether the run's record carries a held{reason: max_crashes}. HEAD instead latches on any item.parked naming the run (runs.rs:268-276), including the SDK's own ask (fleet-z4w).
- `readings` and status's Parked standing take the same answer.
- Each verb's JSON `state` is the entry kind it wrote. review adds "verdict".

Sites (at HEAD bde60be; 6gr's kinds are item.held, hold.cleared, check.read):
- core/src/item/mod.rs:144-180 and :182-242: the item kinds and ITEM_KINDS become `pub const ITEM_ENTRY: &str = "item.entry";`. payload_keys: ITEM_ENTRY => &["item","entry","kind"], and the item rows are deleted. Add `pub fn signal(events: &dyn Events, by: &Actor, item: &str, entry: &str, kind: &str) -> Result<(), String>`.
- The writers switch to signal():
  - dispatch.rs:414-434;
  - deliver.rs:199-232;
  - review.rs:347-370 (accept :331-343, retur :425-435);
  - hold.rs (gate.rs:202-223 and :577-594);
  - run.rs:604-622 (cancel);
  - land.rs:956-977 (the item.landed payload becomes a signal; check.read unchanged).
- controller/src/runs.rs:
  - :50-69, LINES_OF becomes `pub const ITEM_ENTRY: &str = "item.entry";`;
  - :92-108, the Runs trait: `gate` (6gr: `hold`) answers (hold, entry), plus `fn capped(&self, run: &str) -> Result<Option<CapHold>, String>` and `pub struct CapHold { pub hold: String, pub cleared: bool }`;
  - :125-161, Folded.parked and gate: delete;
  - :197-210, the tick at the cap;
  - :268-276, the fold's item.held arm: delete;
  - :304-375, Standing and Reading (gate → hold, plus cleared) and `readings(stream, capped: &BTreeMap<String, CapHold>)`;
  - :466-495, could_wake over ITEM_ENTRY;
  - :497-527, park writes the signal.
- cli/src/runs.rs:
  - :170-195, Engine::gate/hold answers (hold, entry id);
  - a new `capped()`: project_holding, then the last held{MaxCrashes} in the timeline → CapHold{hold, cleared: !open_holds().contains(hold)}.
- cli/src/status.rs:284-306 (read_runs builds the capped map for each run whose last lifecycle line is run.could_not_tell) and :585-600 (the row).
- cli/src/item.rs:796-798 (state()): each verb passes the kind it wrote:
  - dispatch "ordered";
  - deliver "delivered";
  - review "reviewed", with "verdict": "accepted"|"returned";
  - hold "held";
  - clear "cleared";
  - land "landed".
- cli/tests/workspace.rs:160-178: the pairs become (runs::ITEM_ENTRY, item::ITEM_ENTRY).
- core/tests/common/mod.rs:727-745 (keys_agree).
- Tests:
  - controller/tests/runs.rs:231-265 (an_item_moved, a_gate_asked, a_gate_answered), :740-860, :1009-1045;
  - cli/tests/item_json.rs;
  - every core verb suite's event assertions.

Remedy:
1. The signal's actor is the entry's `by`. The payload's entry is the id `recorded` answered. It is written after the read-back and before the exit, and a failure keeps each verb's "STANDS" wording.
2. tick at the cap:
   - `match pass.runs.capped(run)`: Ok(Some(_)) → no park; Ok(None) → park(pass, run, state); Err(why) → a refusal and continue;
   - then clean.
   park writes `item.entry {item: run, entry, kind: "held"}` with actor CONTROLLER.
3. readings(stream, capped): Standing::Parked when the run's last line is run.could_not_tell and capped has the run. Reading.hold and Reading.cleared come from the map. status builds the map through `Engine::on(machine_dir).capped(run)`. An Err on any run → the runs section reads "not all read" and the exit is 3.
4. could_wake Items: `r.kind == ITEM_ENTRY && payload.item ∈ items && payload.kind ∈ kinds && r.seq > since`.

Acceptance:
1. Each verb suite asserts events == [("item.entry", by, {item, entry: <the timeline's entry id>, kind})] through keys_agree(ITEM_ENTRY).
