notes:
DECISION (fleet-alt.1, 2026-09-23): CLEAN BREAK before 0.1.0. No migration of [seats.<name>] tables or seat-list rows; this repo's fleet.toml and machine directory are converted once by hand in the landing.
DESIGN RULED (walkthrough fleet-alt.1 spec pass, 2026-09-23; Alberto, AskUserQuestion, one decision at a time). The inventory is from the research pass at 1b90166; line numbers are that commit's.

RULINGS
R1 A seat's id is a UUID v7, stored whole and shown as an 8-character prefix. A seat has an optional name and a kind (human | agent).
R2 A human's seat is a MACHINE IDENTITY plus a PROJECT ROW. <machine dir>/identity.toml holds {id, kind = "human", name?}. The project's fleet.toml lists seats by id: [seats.<uuid>] with kind, name?, and for agents model and status. `chosen_name` folds into `name`.
R3 THE ACTOR IS A TYPED REFERENCE: {kind: seat | run | routine | controller, id}. Only humans and agents are seats; runs, routines and the controller stay principals of their own. A seat-only check (land's closer, deliver's and ask's holder check, the controller's known-seat fold) refuses a non-seat actor by kind, never by comparing strings.
R4 MACHINE-FACING NAMES ARE <slug>-<8-char id>, e.g. orla-01a0d087, or agent-01a0d09f when unnamed. The slug is the name lowercased and reduced to [a-z0-9-], else the kind. Matching is always on the id part, so a rename moves nothing. This covers worktree directories, per-seat config directories (<machine>/config/), start and nudge logs, and the Claude Code session name (--name).
R5 `fleet seat add` MINTS IDS. `fleet seat add --agent [--name N] [--model M]` and `fleet seat add --human` (the latter defaults to this machine's identity, creating it if absent) write [seats.<uuid>] and read it back. `fleet create` runs the human form for its creator; nobody is asked for a name. A transient seat gets a fresh UUID per spawn, is never reused, and is never written to fleet.toml.
R6 THE DEFAULT ACTOR IS THIS MACHINE'S IDENTITY: with no --by and no FLEET_ACTOR, a writing verb acts as it. If the project does not list that identity, the verb still runs and says once which `fleet seat add --human` lists it. BEADS_ACTOR stops being read (cli/src/item.rs:1165-1175).
R7 CLEAN BREAK before 0.1.0: no migration of [seats.<name>] tables, config.json rows or sessions.json. This repo's fleet.toml and machine directory are converted by hand once in the landing.
Every argument that takes a seat (seat feed/retire/nudge, event woke/rest/handed-off/exited/clear-halt, dispatch/brief --to, status --seat, event tail --seat, [core] reviewer, routine [action.nudge] seat) accepts the full id, a unique 8+ character prefix, or a unique name. An ambiguous name is exit 1 naming the candidates.

