3. Transient naming: claim_transient_seat (config.rs:148-209) mints a UUID instead of the lowest free transient-N, and TRANSIENT_PREFIX goes. retire's withdrawal (core/src/seat/retire.rs) STAYS, because it releases orders so items become dispatchable again. The name-reuse reason in core/src/lib.rs:90-97 is restated.
4. The work graph: the assignee, fleet.orders.seat and fleet.orders.by carry seat ids (or the actor reference for by); `--to` resolves to an id; [core] reviewer resolves to an id; held_item and the dispatch hold check (fleet-pg7) compare ids.
